<article class="prose legal"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Last updated: November 10, 2026</strong></p><p>This Privacy Policy describes the general information practices for Arizona Paycheck Calculator. The site owner should review and adapt this policy to match the services, hosting configuration, analytics, advertising and contact methods actually enabled on the live website.</p><h2>Calculator information</h2><p>Calculator inputs are processed in the visitor’s browser by the current site implementation. The calculator is designed not to transmit or store the figures entered into its fields. Do not enter sensitive personal information such as Social Security numbers, bank details or employer account credentials.</p><h2>Server logs and hosting</h2><p>The hosting provider may process standard technical information such as IP address, browser type, requested URL, referrer and timestamps for security, performance and troubleshooting. The site owner should consult the hosting provider’s current privacy documentation for details about retention and processing.</p><h2>Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2><p>Analytics and advertising are not enabled in the current project configuration. If these services are added later, this policy must be updated to identify the providers, data collected, purposes, cookie controls and any required consent mechanisms before activation.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Pages may link to government agencies and other third-party websites. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies, not this policy.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>This site is intended for a general audience and is not designed to collect personal information from children.</p><h2>Policy updates</h2><p>This policy may be revised when site features or legal requirements change. The revision date above should be updated whenever material changes are made.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for privacy-related questions. A monitored contact address should be added before production launch.</p></article>
